  "probe_findings_that_shape_the_design": [
    "A 64x64 pair is ~32 KB, two to three orders of magnitude below every Activity-side memory metric's noise band. The R10 workload is 4 x 1024x1024 pairs for this reason (V2-R10-DESIGN §4).",
    "X-side metrics are quiet enough to be used directly; Activity-side metrics are not, and require V2-R10-NOISE before they can be judged (§6).",
    "An apparent monotonic rise over five samples (activity.fd_count +1/iteration, gfx_dev +8 KB/iteration) was fully reclaimed at the sixth. A leak verdict from fewer than the full series would have been wrong.",
    "The Activity SURVIVES a clean close (X gone, pid 24987 still running), which is what makes R10-B a real mode rather than a hypothetical one."
  ]
